<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Salamis in Cyprus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">497 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-revolt">Ionian Revolt</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Salamis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> was fought in 497 BCE during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionian-revolt">Ionian Revolt</a>, when the Greek cities of Cyprus, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onesilus">Onesilus of Salamis</a>, rose against Persian rule. An Ionian fleet beat the Phoenician navy at sea, but on land the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> won after Stasanor of Kourion deserted with his troops and the war <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a> of Salamis followed; Onesilus was killed and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> reconquered the island.</p></div>
